			<div class="content" id="post-content-4848348">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The SCP actually refers to multiple anomalies. Or rather, one overarching one. Each anomaly that possesses a physical being, as it turns out, has a counterpart, a mirrored version. A &quot;soulmate&quot; SCP, if you will. When the two SCPs are brought together, they become incredibly powerful, virtually unstoppable, until they are separated once again.</p>
<p>The safest way to contain them is to build a whole Foundation, just for these mirrored versions, keeping them as far away from each other as possible. So that's what the Foundation has done, doubling down on all resources and then splitting themselves in half, effectively forming what is now the SCP Foundation, and the PCS Foundation (Process, Condemn, Shield), run by O5-14 through -26.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Our narrative starts during one of these events where the universe is trying to bring our two foundations back together. The article is initially written about the PCS foundation in general, as SCP staff are, by necessity, unaware of the PCS' existence up until this point. Finding it baffling that PCS has been operating for so long, in such a similar way, without having been discovered before, they are logged as an anomaly, or in possession of an anomaly, or something else entirely. It's left entirely up to theories proposed by the staff.</p>
<p>That is, until the O5 documents, revealing that the entire event was known to be going to happen, that it's happened before, and that even after all SCP and PCS staff are properly amnesticized, they will only discover each other again. This is the Universe trying to have its way, and bringing our mirrored SCPs back together with their originals. Like the mythological tale of humans being split into soulmates, in constant search of each other, so have SCPs.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I'm hoping what draws people in is the concept of a strange, mirrored Foundation, only to eventually reveal that it's not mirrored at all, but rather the same Foundation, forced to split themselves in two.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Below you'll find the initial idea I started with. For the most part, I'm building off it. I'm not sure if I've summarized the new concept as well as I'd like, so feel free to ask questions as need be.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Previous&nbsp;Edit+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Close-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The SCP refers to, what is at first, a hypothetical anomaly. We stumble across a GoI, which operates in an eerily similar fashion to our own Foundation. The PCS Foundation, &quot;Process, Condemn, Shield,&quot; operates with the sole direction of protecting the world from the supernatural, nonsensical, and anomalous. How is it that we've never seen them before?</p>
<p>I'll tell you how. It's us. We ARE the PCS Foundation, and here at the PCS, we contain anomalous soulmates. Every physical SCP has a counterpart. There's the shy guy at the SCP Foundation, here we contain the confident guy. If they ever came together, well, it would form a power-couple of otherworldly proportions. We can't let that happen, so we've split. Once a year, however, something always happens. We always run into each other, like the Universe is trying to glue us back together. So every year a new file is opened about the PCS, and at the PCS, a new file is opened about us. And every year, we burn it, amnesticize all involved, and ready ourselves for next year. Our repeated meetings in themselves are the actual anomaly, and the duration spent investigating each other grows longer, regardless of how much planning ahead is done to prevent it.</p>
<p>What was once one Foundation, is now two. Get ready to meet O5-14 through O5-26.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The narrative is going to follow the first encounter between our SCP Foundation, and the PCS Foundation (Process, Condemn, Shield), and then followed up by a MTF exploration of a PCS facility in hunting for the SCP, then recounting an exact replica of the events that occurred at the PCS facility, except it's an interview recounting the exact same events occurring at a SCP facility. By the end, no actual SCP is recovered, which leads us into the O5 documents, showing a conversation between our O5 council about planning to wipe this year's SCP x PCS crossover clean. The infiltration, it's happened before already. It's not the first time and it won't be the last.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The nature of the anomaly remains unknown, right up until the O5 documents are revealed. One day, we won't be able to keep the two apart anymore. Every year, there's a new problem. It takes longer, and the universe gains more ground in bringing both halves of the foundation back together, in an attempt to recombine skips with their counterparts, their &quot;soulmates.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I know I'm not the greatest at summarizations. It may need some.. work. I'd be happy to clarify anything if the need should be there. Additionally, I sort of jumped the gun and wrote up an unfinished draft. If anyone would like, I'd be happy to let you read it, although it needs some heavy revising.</p>
</div>
