<p>I'm having in-universe theories be proposed as to the nature of the anomaly right off the bat for the reader to contemplate as things move forward.<br />
A few to chew on, if you're curious:<br />
Men in the Mirror - GoI-PCS has avoided detection due to being a recently-formed anomalous group based on the SCP Foundation.</p>
<p>Natural Course - GoI-PCS has avoided detection by adapting the same protocols over time, making them equally as proficient in remaining undetected.</p>
<p>Corporate Espionage - GoI-PCS has avoided detection by gathering information on our protocols and applying these to themselves.</p>
<p>Thaumiel-Esque - GoI-PCS has avoided detection through the use of an anomaly or anomalies that conceal them in some manner, and similarities are coincidental.</p>
<p>And the couple that come up later:</p>
<p>I Am My Greatest Enemy: GoI-PCS is a facility that belonged to the SCP Foundation and was left to rot, then rebuilt itself into its own organization.</p>
<p>Me, Myself, and You: GoI-PCS is a SCP Foundation facility that IS an anomaly, but that anomaly is that it is repeatedly forgotten, then rediscovered. This occurs due to the both of them repeatedly amnesticizing each other.</p>
