<p>So, 1) I don't see an anomaly actually discussed. Sure you're hinting they just appeared&#8230; but there's no specific anomaly at least as how it stands. Do you have an answer? I would suggest making that clear in the post&#8230;</p>
<p>2) I think this would work better as a tale, formatted to read as dueling reports from each organization, finally revealing why it matters to the Foundation or vice versa, that the other exists.</p>
<p>3) I think you're missing stakes/a stinger here. At the end, this is just another GOI that wants the same thing as the Foundation&#8230; So why are you interested in telling this story? What's the ultimate point you're trying to make? As if its merely &quot;other SCP like orgs exist&quot; then I don't see this being satisfying in the end.</p>
<p><em>I have to say that <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;">cybersqyd</a></span>'s suggestion that these are really the same org, and the ultimate revelation is that this has been a mismanagement of an org (foundation) that has just gotten too big to efficiently run its own affairs&#8230; that's fascinating.</em></p>

